{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_stream.go; sed -n '150,250p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_stream_test.go; cat .pose/rules/delivery-evidence.md; rg -n 'TODO|FIXME|stub|panic\\\\(' pose-mcp/internal/cli/change_set_single_pass_test.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/artifact_integrity.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec_trailers.go\"","aggregated_output":"package pose\n\nimport (\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"crypto/sha256\"\n\t\"encoding/hex\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"hash\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"time\"\n)\n\n// Streamed reads (spec pose-read-view-streamed-object-digests): a Git object\n// read whose bytes a producer only hashes is streamed into the producer and\n// the read view retains its digest and length, never its bytes. Streamed\n// bytes have their own budget, apart from the retained captured input.\nconst (\n\t// governanceReadViewMaxStreamedBytes bounds the bytes one operation\n\t// streams, and separately the bytes its final audit streams again.\n\tgovernanceReadViewMaxStreamedBytes = 8 * 1024 * 1024 * 1024\n\t// governanceReadViewMaxStreamedRead bounds one streamed read.\n\tgovernanceReadViewMaxStreamedRead = 256 * 1024 * 1024\n\tgovernanceStreamStderrLimit       = 64 * 1024\n)\n\ntype governanceReadViewStreamObservation struct {\n\troot        string\n\targs        []string\n\tfiles       Files\n\tctx         context.Context\n\tdeadline    time.Time\n\thasDeadline bool\n\tmaxBytes    int64\n\tdigest      string\n\tlength      int64\n\t// errText is the digest of the read's error text, never the text: a\n\t// warning on stderr can be up to the stderr bound, and a retained copy\n\t// per read would escape every budget (review round 2, N2).\n\terrText   string\n\tproducers map[string]bool\n}\n\n// StreamGovernanceRawHistoryGitIn runs a raw-history Git read of an immutable\n// object and streams its output into sink. Inside a governance read view the\n// view records the output's digest and length as the observation and keeps\n// no bytes; reading the same command again in the operation streams it again\n// and leaves the producer unknown if it differs. Outside a view it is a\n// bounded streaming run.\nfunc StreamGovernanceRawHistoryGitIn(files Files, ctx context.Context, root, producer string, maxBytes int64, sink io.Writer, args ...string) error {\n\tif maxBytes <= 0 || maxBytes > governanceReadViewMaxStreamedRead {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"pose: streamed Git output limit must be between 1 and %d bytes\", governanceReadViewMaxStreamedRead)\n\t}\n\tif ctx == nil {\n\t\tctx = context.Background()\n\t}\n\tfiles = FilesOrNative(files)\n\tview, viewFiles := governanceReadViewFromFiles(files)\n\tif view == nil {\n\t\t_, _, _, err := runGovernanceGitStreamContext(ctx, files, root, args, maxBytes, nil, sink)\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tif view.operation == nil {\n\t\tview.markUnknown(producer, \"Git input has no operation-scoped generation vector\")\n\t\t_, _, _, err := runGovernanceGitStreamContext(ctx, files, root, args, maxBytes, nil, sink)\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tif viewFiles != nil {\n\t\tif target := view.route(root, producer, viewFiles.project); target == nil {\n\t\t\tview.markUnknown(producer, \"Git input is outside the authorized root generation vector\")\n\t\t\treturn errGovernanceReadViewOutsideRoot\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tview = target\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\top := view.operation\n\tabsolute, target, state, err := op.gitRoot(root, producer)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tif err := target.begin(); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tdefer target.end()\n\treturn state.stream(files, ctx, absolute, producer, maxBytes, sink, args...)\n}\n\nfunc (op *governanceReadViewOperation) reserveStreamed(size int64) bool {\n\tif op == nil {\n\t\treturn size >= 0 && size <= governanceReadViewMaxStreamedBytes\n\t}\n\tif size < 0 {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\top.budgetMu.Lock()\n\tdefer op.budgetMu.Unlock()\n\tif size > governanceReadViewMaxStreamedBytes-op.streamedBytes {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\top.streamedBytes += size\n\treturn true\n}\n\nfunc (state *governanceReadViewGitState) stream(files Files, ctx context.Context, root, producer string, maxBytes int64, sink io.Writer, args ...string) error {\n\tdeadline, hasDeadline := ctx.Deadline()\n\tkey := governanceGitObservationKey(root, args, maxBytes)\n\tstate.mu.Lock()\n\tif state.streams == nil {\n\t\tstate.streams = map[string]*governanceReadViewStreamObservation{}\n\t}\n\tprior := state.streams[key]\n\tif prior == nil {\n\t\tmetadataCost := int64(len(root) + len(key) + len(producer) + 128)\n\t\tif !state.op.reserveRecord(metadataCost) {\n\t\t\tstate.mu.Unlock()\n\t\t\tstate.markUnknownForRoot(root, producer, \"read view exceeded its shared record or metadata budget while streaming Git\")\n\t\t\treturn errGovernanceReadViewBudget\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tstate.mu.Unlock()\n\tdigest, length, stderr, runErr := governanceStreamRun(ctx, files, root, args, maxBytes, state.op.reserveStreamed, sink)\n\tif errors.Is(runErr, errGovernanceReadViewBudget) {\n\t\tstate.markUnknownForRoot(root, producer, \"Git streamed output exceeded the read-view streamed byte budget\")\n\t\treturn errGovernanceReadViewBudget\n\t}\n\t_ = stderr\n\tstate.mu.Lock()\n\tif prior = state.streams[key]; prior != nil {\n\t\tprior.producers[producer] = true\n\t\tsame := prior.digest == digest && prior.length == length && prior.errText == streamErrorDigest(runErr)\n\t\tstate.mu.Unlock()\n\t\tif !same {\n\t\t\tstate.markUnknownForRoot(root, producer, \"a streamed Git object read differed within the operation\")\n\t\t\treturn errGovernanceReadViewBudget\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn runErr\n\t}\n\tstate.streams[key] = &governanceReadViewStreamObservation{\n\t\troot: root, args: append([]string(nil), args...), files: files, ctx: context.WithoutCancel(ctx), deadline: deadline, hasDeadline: hasDeadline,\n\t\tmaxBytes: maxBytes, digest: digest, length: length, errText: streamErrorDigest(runErr), producers: map[string]bool{producer: true},\n\t}\n\tstate.mu.Unlock()\n\treturn runErr\n}\n\n// auditStreams streams every observation again, under its own audit budget,\n// and reports a producer changed when the digest, length or error differs.\nfunc (state *governanceReadViewGitState) auditStreams(result *governanceReadViewAudit) {\n\tstate.mu.Lock()\n\tstreams := make([]governanceReadViewStreamObservation, 0, len(state.streams))\n\tfor _, item := range state.streams {\n\t\tcopy := *item\n\t\tcopy.args = append([]string(nil), item.args...)\n\t\tcopy.producers = cloneBoolMap(item.producers)\n\t\tstreams = append(streams, copy)\n\t}\n\tstate.mu.Unlock()\n\tsort.Slice(streams, func(i, j int) bool {\n\t\treturn governanceGitObservationKey(streams[i].root, streams[i].args, streams[i].maxBytes) < governanceGitObservationKey(streams[j].root, streams[j].args, streams[j].maxBytes)\n\t})\n\tvar budgetMu sync.Mutex\n\tremaining := int64(governanceReadViewMaxStreamedBytes)\n\tadmit := func(size int64) bool {\n\t\tbudgetMu.Lock()\n\t\tdefer budgetMu.Unlock()\n\t\tif size < 0 || size > remaining {\n\t\t\treturn false\n\t\t}\n\t\tremaining -= size\n\t\treturn true\n\t}\n\t// Every streamed read is streamed again: its rendering depends on Git\n\t// configuration and attributes the operation does not capture, so no\n\t// read is proven unchanged without it (review round 1, F1 and F3).\n\tfor _, item := range streams {\n\t\tauditContext := item.ctx\n\t\tcancel := func() {}\n\t\tif item.hasDeadline {\n\t\t\tauditContext, cancel = context.WithDeadline(auditContext, item.deadline)\n\t\t}\n\t\tdigest, length, _, err := governanceAuditGitStream(auditContext, item.files, item.root, item.args, item.maxBytes, admit, io.Discard)\n\t\tcancel()\n\t\tif errors.Is(err, errGovernanceReadViewBudget) {\n\t\t\tfor producer := range item.producers {\n\t\t\t\tresult.UnknownProducers[producer] = appendUnique(result.UnknownProducers[producer], \"Git streamed final audit exceeded its byte budget\")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif digest != item.digest || length != item.length || streamErrorDigest(err) != item.errText {\n\t\t\tfor producer := range item.producers {\n\t\t\t\tresult.ChangedProducers[producer] = true\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\trootDigest := digestBytes([]byte(filepath.Clean(item.root)))\n\t\t\targsDigest := digestBytes([]byte(strings.Join(item.args, \"\\x00\")))\n\t\t\tresult.ChangedPaths = append(result.ChangedPaths, \"git:\"+strings.TrimPrefix(rootDigest, \"sha256:\")+\":\"+strings.TrimPrefix(argsDigest, \"sha256:\"))\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\n// governanceStreamRun and governanceAuditGitStream run streamed reads during\n// the operation and in its final audit.\nvar (\n\tgovernanceStreamRun      = runGovernanceGitStreamContext\n\tgovernanceAuditGitStream = runGovernanceGitStreamContext\n)\n\n// runGovernanceGitStreamContext runs Git like the captured reads do and\n// writes its stdout to sink as it arrives, admitting each chunk before it is\n// written and hashing it; stderr is kept bounded. It returns the stdout's\n// digest and length. A non-empty stderr is an error, as for captured reads.\nfunc runGovernanceGitStreamContext(ctx context.Context, files Files, root string, args []string, limit int64, admit func(int64) bool, sink io.Writer) (string, int64, []byte, error) {\n\tif limit <= 0 {\n\t\treturn \"\", 0, nil, errGovernanceReadViewBudget\n\t}\n\t_ = FilesOrNative(files)\n\tif ctx == nil {\n\t\tctx = context.Background()\n\t}\n\tif sink == nil {\n\t\tsink = io.Discard\n\t}\n\tcmd := gitCommandContext(ctx, append([]string{\"--no-replace-objects\", \"-C\", root}, args...)...)\n\tcmd.WaitDelay = 2 * time.Second\n\tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Env, \"GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0\")\n\tout := &governanceStreamWriter{limit: limit, admit: admit, sink: sink, hash: sha256.New()}\n\tvar stderr bytes.Buffer\n\tcmd.Stdout = out\n\tcmd.Stderr = &limitedStderr{buf: &stderr, limit: governanceStreamStderrLimit}\n\terr := cmd.Run()\n\tif out.exceeded {\n\t\treturn \"\", 0, nil, errGovernanceReadViewBudget\n\t}\n\tdigest := \"sha256:\" + hex.EncodeToString(out.hash.Sum(nil))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif exit, ok := err.(*exec.ExitError); ok {\n\t\t\texit.Stderr = append([]byte(nil), stderr.Bytes()...)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn digest, out.written, stderr.Bytes(), &GitSnapshotError{Operation: strings.Join(args, \" \"), Cause: err}\n\t}\n\tif stderr.Len() > 0 {\n\t\tdetail := strings.TrimSpace(stderr.String())\n\t\tif detail == \"\" {\n\t\t\tdetail = \"Git wrote unclassified stderr output\"\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn digest, out.written, stderr.Bytes(), &GitSnapshotError{Operation: strings.Join(args, \" \"), Cause: errors.New(detail)}\n\t}\n\treturn digest, out.written, nil, nil\n}\n\ntype governanceStreamWriter struct {\n\tmu       sync.Mutex\n\tlimit    int64\n\twritten  int64\n\tadmit    func(int64) bool\n\tsink     io.Writer\n\thash     hash.Hash\n\texceeded bool\n}\n\nfunc (w *governanceStreamWriter) Write(data []byte) (int, error) {\n\tw.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer w.mu.Unlock()\n\tif w.exceeded || int64(len(data)) > w.limit-w.written || w.admit != nil && !w.admit(int64(len(data))) {\n\t\tw.exceeded = true\n\t\treturn 0, errGovernanceReadViewBudget\n\t}\n\tif _, err := w.sink.Write(data); err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, err\n\t}\n\tw.hash.Write(data)\n\tw.written += int64(len(data))\n\treturn len(data), nil\n}\n\ntype limitedStderr struct {\n\tbuf   *bytes.Buffer\n\tlimit int\n}\n\nfunc (w *limitedStderr) Write(data []byte) (int, error) {\n\tif room := w.limit - w.buf.Len(); room > 0 {\n\t\tif len(data) > room {\n\t\t\tw.buf.Write(data[:room])\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tw.buf.Write(data)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn len(data), nil\n}\n\n// streamErrorDigest is the fixed-size identity of a streamed read's error.\nfunc streamErrorDigest(err error) string {\n\tif err == nil {\n\t\treturn \"\"\n\t}\n\treturn digestBytes([]byte(errorText(err)))\n}\n\tvar reruns atomic.Int64\n\toriginal := governanceAuditGitStream\n\tgovernanceAuditGitStream = func(ctx context.Context, files Files, r string, args []string, limit int64, admit func(int64) bool, sink io.Writer) (string, int64, []byte, error) {\n\t\treruns.Add(1)\n\t\treturn original(ctx, files, r, args, limit, admit, sink)\n\t}\n\tdefer func() { governanceAuditGitStream = original }()\n\tread := func() *governanceReadView {\n\t\tbase, view := (Store{Root: root}).beginGovernanceReadView()\n\t\tstore := base.withGovernanceReadView(view, \"stream-audit\")\n\t\tif err := StreamGovernanceRawHistoryGitIn(store.fsys(), context.Background(), root, \"stream-audit\", 1<<20, io.Discard, streamArgs(id)...); err != nil {\n\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn view\n\t}\n\tif audit := read().audit(); reruns.Load() != 1 || audit.ChangedProducers[\"stream-audit\"] {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an unchanged read was not streamed again or did not pass: reruns=%d %+v\", reruns.Load(), audit)\n\t}\n\tview := read()\n\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"info\", \"attributes\"), []byte(\"a.md -diff\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tif audit := view.audit(); reruns.Load() != 2 || !audit.ChangedProducers[\"stream-audit\"] {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an attribute that changed the rendered patch was not found: reruns=%d %+v\", reruns.Load(), audit)\n\t}\n}\n\n// Two first reads of the same command that run concurrently and differ\n// leave the producer unknown (review round 1, F2).\nfunc TestConcurrentFirstStreamedReadsAreCompared(t *testing.T) {\n\troot, id := streamTestRepo(t)\n\tbase, view := (Store{Root: root}).beginGovernanceReadView()\n\tstore := base.withGovernanceReadView(view, \"stream-race\")\n\tvar calls atomic.Int64\n\tstarted := make(chan struct{}, 2)\n\trelease := make(chan struct{})\n\toriginal := governanceStreamRun\n\tgovernanceStreamRun = func(ctx context.Context, files Files, r string, args []string, limit int64, admit func(int64) bool, sink io.Writer) (string, int64, []byte, error) {\n\t\tn := calls.Add(1)\n\t\tstarted <- struct{}{}\n\t\t<-release\n\t\tbody := []byte(\"read \" + string(rune('0'+n)))\n\t\t_, _ = sink.Write(body)\n\t\treturn digestBytes(body), int64(len(body)), nil, nil\n\t}\n\tdefer func() { governanceStreamRun = original }()\n\terrs := make(chan error, 2)\n\tfor i := 0; i < 2; i++ {\n\t\tgo func() {\n\t\t\terrs <- StreamGovernanceRawHistoryGitIn(store.fsys(), context.Background(), root, \"stream-race\", 1<<20, io.Discard, streamArgs(id)...)\n\t\t}()\n\t}\n\t<-started\n\t<-started\n\tclose(release)\n\tfailed := 0\n\tfor i := 0; i < 2; i++ {\n\t\tif err := <-errs; err != nil {\n\t\t\tfailed++\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tmetadata, _ := view.metadata(store.FederatedProjectID, \"\", \"\", view.audit())\n\tif failed != 1 || !strings.Contains(strings.Join(metadata.Limitations, \"\\n\"), \"differed within the operation\") {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"concurrent differing first reads both succeeded: failed=%d limitations=%v\", failed, metadata.Limitations)\n\t}\n}\n\n// Review round 2 (N2): a read whose stderr carries a long warning retains a\n// fixed-size digest of the error, not its text.\nfunc TestAStreamedReadWarningIsRetainedAsADigest(t *testing.T) {\n\troot, id := streamTestRepo(t)\n\tbase, view := (Store{Root: root}).beginGovernanceReadView()\n\tstore := base.withGovernanceReadView(view, \"stream-warning\")\n\twarning := strings.Repeat(\"w\", governanceStreamStderrLimit)\n\toriginal := governanceStreamRun\n\tgovernanceStreamRun = func(ctx context.Context, files Files, r string, args []string, limit int64, admit func(int64) bool, sink io.Writer) (string, int64, []byte, error) {\n\t\treturn digestBytes(nil), 0, []byte(warning), &GitSnapshotError{Operation: strings.Join(args, \" \"), Cause: errors.New(warning)}\n\t}\n\tdefer func() { governanceStreamRun = original }()\n\tif err := StreamGovernanceRawHistoryGitIn(store.fsys(), context.Background(), root, \"stream-warning\", 1<<20, io.Discard, streamArgs(id)...); err == nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"a read with a warning succeeded\")\n\t}\n\tfor _, item := range view.operation.git.streams {\n\t\tif len(item.errText) > 80 || item.errText == \"\" {\n\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the warning was retained as %d bytes\", len(item.errText))\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n# Rule: Delivery Evidence\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide when writing or reviewing any document that **claims delivery,\ncompletion, or readiness**: status reports, handoffs, summaries, module READMEs,\ncurrent-state sections in specs or proposals, and messages that say something is complete.\n\n## Required conventions\n\n- Claim delivery only with attached, verifiable gate evidence: command and output\n  (`pose validate`, `go test`, `tsc`, `vitest`) or a link to the corresponding POSE report.\n- Use POSE lifecycle vocabulary: `draft`, `in-progress`, `done`, `blocked`,\n  `superseded`, or `abandoned`. Do not invent labels such as `completed` or `100% COMPLETE`.\n- Separate **implemented and verified** work from **planned or documented** work.\n  A plan describes intent; do not present that intent as current reality.\n- Reference the report or evidence that crossed the spec exit gate before using `done`.\n- Convert relative dates to absolute dates and stamp the verification date.\n- Declare exact source-tree artifact actions in the spec and reconcile them\n  against an immutable Git change set before claiming delivery.\n- Treat artifact declarations, Git observations and delivery verification as\n  separate evidence; none proves the others by itself.\n- For typed delivery targets, require a path from reconciled artifacts through\n  a production entrypoint to current structured validation results. A surface\n  requires reachability plus integration/e2e evidence; a composed capability\n  requires integration evidence.\n- Evidence answers for the component it ran in or for a component inside it: a\n  module-wide run covers its subtree, but a result from a directory inside a\n  component does not answer for the whole component. Coverage that rests only\n  on a containing module is reported as `inferred-coverage` — name it as such.\n\n## Blocking anti-patterns\n\n- Claiming `100% COMPLETE` or production readiness without a green\n  `pose validate --strict` for every affected module.\n- Publishing contradictory delivery documents for the same scope; reconcile them first.\n- Merging code with completion documentation before the applicable POSE checks pass.\n- Mixing aspiration and verified state in one paragraph without clear labels.\n\n## Minimum checks\n\n- Run `pose check --strict` for structure and spec status enums.\n- Run `pose validate --strict` for every module the document claims to deliver.\n- Run `pose lint-spec` when the document is a spec.\n- Run `pose artifact-check --strict` when the scope changes governed source-tree paths.\n- Run `pose surface-check --strict` for specs with `delivers` and `pose\n  roadmap-check --strict` before a roadmap claims completion.\n- `pose assess discover --if-stale --update-state` when closing specs to update completeness metrics, technical debt, and reports under `.pose/assessments/` and `.pose/state/`.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence over progress narratives when rules conflict.\n- When pressured to claim completion without a gate, record the real state\n  (`in-progress` or `blocked`) and the remaining exit conditions.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
