{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: approved\n\nNo defect found in the scoped implementation. One pre-existing, low-severity test portability defect is accepted as a follow-up.\n\nThe focused tests, artifact-check, and surface-check passed. The broader run passed `internal/pose` and `internal/mcpserver`; CLI failed because `findingIsAWarning` rejects the Unicode warning prefix `⚠`. The helper is unchanged from the base commit.\n\nApplied rules: backend-go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence. Reviewed bundle `rvb-3bc3836818140841` against the supplied review-brief/7 plan. No repository changes or attestation were made.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F1\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/check_index_generation_test.go\",\n      \"line\": 85,\n      \"summary\": \"Pre-existing test portability defect: findingIsAWarning accepts only ASCII warning prefixes. Under a UTF-8 locale, cmdCheck correctly emits '⚠ warning', but TestCheckRefusesAnIndexSetThatItsDescriptorDoesNotDescribe fails at line 47. Reproduced both in the broader test run and in isolation; git show of the base commit confirms the helper is unchanged. This does not invalidate the single-pass implementation or the sealed validation results.\",\n      \"action\": \"Make the warning assertion independent of rendering profile, or explicitly select a deterministic profile and cover the Unicode form.\",\n      \"owner\": \"POSE maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-14\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/index-streams-each-commit-once-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared both trailer parsers and verified the shared-order subsequence premise in spec_trailers.go:31-66. Independently ran digest-equivalence, read-count, and failed-stream tests. Corpus byte-identity and timing remain implementer-reported measurements, not independently repeated benchmarks. Duplicate trailers deliberately retain per-spec reads. The local broader-test failure is the pre-existing rendering assertion recorded as F1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The new hash maps and writers are local to a synchronous collection call. No goroutines or shared mutable state were introduced. changeSetGitStream preserves the timeout, cancellation cleanup, and existing read-view lifecycle.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/index-streams-each-commit-once-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Digest computation and change-set construction retain their existing formulas and fields; only internal patch acquisition changes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-streamed-object-digests-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed existing slug and revision validation, bounded history and patch reads, and error wrapping. artifact_integrity.go:466-478 excludes failed digests; lines 676-678 preserve the cause as a collection gap. The failed-stream regression passed locally.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-operation-performance-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The production collector invokes the shared pass at artifact_integrity.go:673 and consumes its digests at line 680. The collector performance test exercises this composition for multiple specs and passed locally.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-streamed-object-digests-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The extracted stream helper retains bounded stderr and wrapped forensic causes. Collection errors retain spec context, and failed partial hashes are not published.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/index-streams-each-commit-once-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined parser semantics, Git arguments, digest substitution, and returned ChangeSet fields. Public CLI, MCP, and serialized file contracts remain unchanged; duplicate trailer semantics are preserved through fallback.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-3948ef79d5b82523\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 selects ordered fan-out because repeated patch reads arise from per-spec collection. artifact_integrity.go:437-478 streams each eligible commit into all owning hashes, addressing R1 without retaining patch bytes. Duplicate detection implements R3; the resolver consumes the precomputed digest for R2; failure fan-out and collection gaps implement R4. No individual structural-fact deltas were supplied in the brief.\",\n      \"mappings\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/validation-matrix-run-patterns-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the spec, implementation comments, and validation-matrix addition. The SinglePass selector matches the new test. Documentation accurately describes duplicate-trailer fallback, unchanged final audit, and absence of persistent caching.\"\n    },\n 