ef79d5b82523\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared D1's alternatives. Ordered MultiWriter fan-out is sufficient because every spec's commit sequence derives from the same log; retaining patch bytes or persisting digests would add unnecessary storage and invalidation concerns. The duplicate-trailer fallback avoids a more complex replay mechanism. Revisit this choice if attribution sequences cease to be subsequences of one shared log.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-index-streams-each-commit-once --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran successfully with exit code 0. A second JSON run confirmed no error or critical findings. Existing provenance warnings and later refs visible through --all were distinguished from the sealed implementation range.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed D1, implementation structure, and sealed structure:design-3948ef79d5b82523. Did not rerun the assessment because repository writes are prohibited.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Component discovery was unnecessary to resolve the explicitly supplied component and implementation paths. Did not run an assessment that writes repository state.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"No public API, event, schema, or MCP contract changes were found. Reviewed production collector composition, read-view integration, and sealed integration evidence without writing assessment artifacts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not run the state-writing assessment. Inspected the changed code and searched the affected implementation files for TODO, FIXME, stub, and panic markers; none were found there.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Requires the completed review attestation. Recording an attestation is explicitly outside this independent review.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Requires POSE to record this review conclusion first; no attestation was recorded.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Selected backend-go, security, and documentation-style rules; also applied delivery-evidence to delivery claims.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/index-streams-each-commit-once-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran pose surface-check --spec pose-index-streams-each-commit-once --strict: exit 0, one target, zero findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Accepted the sealed producer execution of strict validation. Inspected delivery-validation.json: 215 executed, 215 passed, zero failures. Did not rerun the repository-writing validation command. Independent broader tests exposed the pre-existing locale-sensitive assertion recorded as F1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed sealed pose-mcp build, unit, and integration results from strict validation. Component coverage is supplied by that containing validation run. Independently reran focused single-pass, failed-stream, 